#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 960.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222332} :activity/id #uuid "bf2387fe-ebed-5568-a260-0d681cb9fd28" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050228 :topic/id #uuid "37d183d8-ce59-581c-9a89-fec7544aae03" :topic/math-academy-id 6376} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222332 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222502 :tutorial/content "Consider the homogeneous linear system\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}' = A\\mathbf{x},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix.\n\nA **fundamental matrix** for this system is an $n\\times n$ matrix $\\Phi(t)$ whose columns are $n$ linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIf $\\mathbf{x}_1(t),\\dots,\\mathbf{x}_n(t)$ are linearly independent solutions, then one fundamental matrix is\n\n$$\n\\Phi(t)=\\big[\\mathbf{x}_1(t),\\dots,\\mathbf{x}_n(t)\\big].\n$$\n\n**Note:** The columns of $\\Phi(t)$ can be written in any order.\n\nLet's see an example." :tutorial/id #uuid "a7207a24-194d-59d6-b25c-f9bb4f1b0d6e" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14508 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "3b0bd285-b383-5ebb-821f-4f74a0b37719" :step/math-academy-id 594316 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222333}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222333 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221420 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221191 :question/id #uuid "4874a486-2cf1-5b6e-ae4f-52579f03b077" :question/math-academy-id "e-21695"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "af871f3d-da9e-5fd3-a61f-94e155ccf2b3" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049851}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221985} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221999} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308599} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308600} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308601} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398781} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442556} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442557} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442562}] :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Fundamental Matrix"} :step/id #uuid "aa3c7790-3ab9-5519-bad3-4f82fc8ac113" :step/math-academy-id 594317 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222334}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222334 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222503 :tutorial/content "Again, let $\\Phi(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for the linear system\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}' = A\\mathbf{x},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix. The fundamental matrices have the following important properties.\n\n1\\. *Satisfies the underlying system*. Indeed, since each column of $\\Phi(t)$ is a solution of the system, we have\n\n  $$\n  \\Phi'(t) = A\\,\\Phi(t).\n  $$\n\n2\\. *Invertibility*. The columns of $\\Phi(t)$ are linearly independent for all $t,$ so\n\n  $$\n  \\det\\Phi(t)\\neq 0\n  $$\n\n  for all $t.$ In particular, $\\Phi(t)$ is invertible for all $t.$\n\n3\\. *Representation of solutions*. Every solution $\\mathbf{x}(t)$ of the system can be written in the form\n\n  $$\n  \\mathbf{x}(t)=\\Phi(t)\\,\\mathbf{c},\n  $$\n\n  where $\\mathbf{c}$ is a constant vector.\n\n4\\. *Non-uniqueness*. If $C$ is any invertible constant matrix, then\n\n  $$\n  \\Psi(t)=\\Phi(t)\\,C\n  $$\n\n  is also a fundamental matrix for the same system.\n\nWe'll now get some practice." :tutorial/id #uuid "e2fdbc29-4542-5fdc-adbd-316c5dcb6878" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14509 :tutorial/title "Properties of the Fundamental Matrix"} :step/id #uuid "2fe7252e-7fc7-59bb-bc32-74c452b7cf73" :step/math-academy-id 594320 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222335}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222335 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221421 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221193 :question/id #uuid "a52a6539-60d1-557c-a042-cbce5616e94f" :question/math-academy-id "e-21697"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0aea7503-74d6-5ba4-9411-ee53e59512d0" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221990} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221991} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311648} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311687} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365731} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391264} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396895} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396916} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442561}] :knowledge-point/title "Proving Properties of a Fundamental Matrix"} :step/id #uuid "2b90cd12-9695-5b6b-b407-6eed6ae7fc84" :step/math-academy-id 594321 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222336}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222336 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222504 :tutorial/content "For a linear system $\\mathbf{x}' = A\\mathbf{x}$ with constant $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ the **standard fundamental matrix** is the unique fundamental matrix $\\Phi_0(t)$ that satisfies the initial condition\n\n$$\n\\Phi_0(0)=I_n,\n$$\n\nwhere $I_n$ is the $n \\times n$ identity matrix.\n\nFor constant matrices $A,$ the standard fundamental matrix is given by\n\n$$\n\\Phi_0(t)=e^{At}.\n$$\n\nThis matrix satisfies\n\n$$\n\\Phi_0'(t)=A\\,\\Phi_0(t)\n\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\n\\Phi_0(0)=I_n.\n$$\n\n**Note:** Any other fundamental matrix $\\Phi(t)$ for the same system can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\Phi(t)=\\Phi_0(t)\\,C,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an invertible constant matrix.\n\nIn the next slide, we will compute the standard fundamental matrix for a specific example." :tutorial/id #uuid "4f75576c-be32-5784-9fee-e1288445728c" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14510 :tutorial/title "Fundamental Matrices and Matrix Exponentials"} :step/id #uuid "d44c84d5-4215-5318-bba2-81eb3a34ee7d" :step/math-academy-id 594325 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222337}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222337 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221422 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221192 :question/id #uuid "3e053d6d-f051-5c4c-a20b-1e90b2d5941b" :question/math-academy-id "e-21696"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "66c99cda-25a5-50f2-903b-bfb1fdc5fa10" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050054}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221988} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221989} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308497} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308609} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308611} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308634} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365659} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365668} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365673} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442558} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442559} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442560}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing Fundamental Matrices Using Matrix Exponentials"} :step/id #uuid "32e0e465-9256-5f88-b771-2edff24ecd54" :step/math-academy-id 594326}] :activity/title "Fundamental Matrices" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186221468}]}
